<title>UK: O'Donnell appointed HSBC James Capel CEO.</title>
<headline>O'Donnell appointed HSBC James Capel CEO.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jim O'Donnell, the president of HSBC Markets Inc, will also now become chief executive officer of HSBC James Capel from July 1, banking giant HSBC Group said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Former CEO Peter Letley, the deputy chairman of HSBC Investment Bank Plc, will therefore relinquish his chief executive responsibilities so he can concentrate on his other duties in the investment banking division.</p>
</text>
